rvation: a role for rice farmers</article-title><source>Plant Genetic conservation-the in situ approach</source><year>1997</year><publisher-name>Chapman &#x00026; Hall, London</publisher-name><fpage>263</fpage><lpage>289</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brush</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Brokensha DW, Warren DM, Werner 0</surname></name></person-group><source>Potato taxonomies in Andean agriculture Indigenous Knowledge Systems and Development</source><year>1980</year><publisher-name>The University Press of America, New York</publisher-name><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><comment>37&#x02013;47</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brush</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Carney</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Haumam</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dynamics of Andean potato agriculture</article-title><source>Economic Botany</source><year>1981</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>70</fpage><lpage>85</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Alcorn</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><source>Huastec Mayan Ethnobotany</source><year>1984</year><publisher-name>Univ. Texas Press, Austin</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hernandez</surname><given-names>XE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Maize and man in the greater southwest</article-title><source>Economic Botany</source><year>1985</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>416</fpage><lpage>430</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-typ