 esculenta</italic></article-title><source>Economic Botany</source><year>1985</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>310</fpage><lpage>325</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B35"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>ICRISAT/IBPGR</collab></person-group><source>Descriptors for sorghum (Sorghum bicolor (L) Moench)</source><year>1993</year><publisher-name>International Board for Plant Genetic Resources, Rome; International Crops Research Institute for the Semiarid Tropics, A.P., India</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B36"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Plant Genetic Resources Centre/Ethiopia</collab></person-group><source>Ten years of collection, conservation and utilization, 1976&#x02013;86</source><year>1986</year><publisher-name>PGRC/E, Addis Ababa, Ethiopia</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B37"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mekbib</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic erosion of sorghum (<italic>Sorghum bicolor </italic>(L.) Moench) in the center of diversity, Ethiopia</article-title><source>Genetic Resources and Crop Evolution</source><year>2007</year><comment>10.1007/s10722-007-9240-7</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B38"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boster</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Selection for perceptual distinctiveness: evidence from traditional farming system</article-title><source>Economic Botany</source><year>1984</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>34</fpage><lpage>47</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>